{
  "name": "11-limit-handoff-no-rules",
  "description": "Trace 05's commands in a workspace with no rules: a run hits a provider limit after one criterion has passed and hands off at once to the next login below it, of another provider; that one hits its limit too, so the task is held with credential_limit and waits for the seat's own login, which resets first; the hold-release timer closes the hold at the reset time and the work goes back to the seat's own login; the builder passes the second criterion and a reviewer on a third provider passes the task.",
  "covers": [
    "PRD test 8 and Build order, Handoff: one of the five golden traces for a workspace with no rules (milestone 3 plan HT-1, PRD R-7).",
    "PRD Handoff, When a run hits a provider limit: credential.limit_reached, then credential.switched in the same command with the app as actor and the helper's key (plan IF-37); the login above the seat's own is not tried.",
    "PRD Handoff, Which model continues: a handoff to another provider uses the credential's model, which is empty for a Codex login (milestone 3 plan HE-5), so the payload's model is null; going back to the seat's own provider uses the seat's model.",
    "PRD Handoff, Waiting on a limit: credential_limit with no Needs you item while a reset time is known; hold.opened and the wait_limit step name the candidate that resets first (milestone 3 plan rule 6 of section 2.1); the lease keeps running.",
    "Milestone 3 plan rule 8 of section 2.1 and HE-23: credential_hold_release is due at the earliest reset among the signed-in candidates and records hold.closed at that time; credential.switched follows because the seat's own login is not the one last recorded for the task.",
    "PRD Recovery time and milestone 3 plan HE-17: 0 seconds for the first limit (the switch in the same command) and 1600 seconds for the second (@t:900 to the seat's criterion.passed at @t:2500); the timer's events are the app's and end nothing.",
    "PRD Rules for steps, rule 8: a handoff with no hold opens no new step; the hold interrupts build and build comes back with its criterion when the hold lifts."
  ],
